==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 0.67~20 seconds<sup>20f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Bore]] spawns as the boss.

==Strategy==
In your lineup, equip typical anti-Red Cats, including ones that can weaken, knockback, and slow, as you are going to face the Bore. When the battle starts, gain money by sending out a few [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Wall Cats]] to stall the enemies. When you have a wallet that is at least level 5 or more and almost full, send out [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], along with [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho]], Wall, and [[Axe Cat (Normal Cat)|Brave]] Cats. If you can, send out [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon]] and [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs]] just to be safe. Once the base takes enough damage, the Bore should appear. Keep sending out Macho, Wall and Brave to stall the Bore, along with ranged attackers. By now, you should've beaten the Bore and now you can freely attack the base and win.

If you possess [[Pirate Cat (Rare Cat)|Pirate Cat]] this should be a fairly easy battle. Start off by stalling the Gories as long as you can with Tank Cat and Macho Cat. Keep stalling until you can afford the Bahamut Cat. Keep protecting the Bahamut Cat as he slowly pushes. Start sending out Pirate Cats. One you have a fair amount of money send out everything you have pushing to the base.

It's recommended that you bring long range Cats like Sexy legs, Dragon Cat and Paris Cat. Keep attacking the base, and remember to send out Pirate Cat as soon as you can. Once the Bore appears, he should be getting knocked back every few seconds and not getting any chances to hit your units.

